lative 1e-9. *Owner:* Wave 24 (corpus) + Wave 25 (scoring). *Terminus:* the Wave-25 done-when asserts all per-class floors + kâ€².\n- **Metric G + canned baseline (the oracle gate)** â€” *value:* **G = catch-rate âˆ’ false-positive-rate** over the canonical **SCORED SUBSET** (= the planted-defect computational/firewall fixtures; the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset is EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator and feeds only the FP/kâ€² term â€” the SAME token is used verbatim in the Wave-25 done-when). The canned baseline is PINNED as TWO stub scorers â€” **always-ABSTAIN** and **always-FLAG** â€” scored on the identical SCORED SUBSET with G computed by the identical formula; **acceptance = G(battery-on) > G(better stub) + 0.30 (strict)** AND the ablation arm scores measurably lower; **ABSTAIN-correctness floor = 100%** of proof/conceptual arms ABSTAIN. *Owner:* Wave 25. *Terminus:* the Wave-25 done-when cites the SCORED SUBSET token, the two stub baselines, the 0.30 epsilon, the per-class floors, kâ€², and the 100% abstain floor.\n- **S1 (CONTROL thresholds + gap-function)** â€” *value:* budget = 8 steps; gap-function = no progress-boolean=true in the last m=3 steps â‡’ switch; 2 consecutive switches â‡’ ABANDON; on the pinned canned non-converging fixture ABANDON fires via the gap-function **strictly before step 8** (reason=gap-function, never budget-exhausted). *Owner:* Wave 17. *Terminus:* the ABANDON fixture exits reason=gap-function before step 8, claim left UNVERIFIED.\n- **S4 (ref-fn-independence invariant)** â€” *value:* a firewall ref-fn whose AST shares no symbol-provenance with the comprehension narrative; else cap at CLAIMED. *Owner:* Wave 11. *Terminus:* the planted-wrong-same-family-reference fixture caps at CLAIMED.\n- **P3 (example-space-stability predicate)** â€” *value:* ADVISORY-only; \"stable\" = no new monster in the last r=2 example-rounds; never gates promotion. *Owner:* Wave 20. *Terminus:* a forged-but-unfaithful but example-stable definition still stamps requires-Phase-F.\n- **P7 (default-deny grammar + battery + recall roster + closure)** â€” *value:* a CLOSED whitelist grammar over EXACT arithmetic (numeric literals; finite arithmetic ops; bounded finite sums/products with literal bounds; NO float/symbolic/unbounded/quantified nodes); â‰¥8 positive-recall computations (incl. â‰¥1 nested-composition) it MUST settle; â‰¥8 smuggled-non-literal inputs (incl. â‰¥1 deep-nested-smuggle) it MUST reject. *Owner:* Wave 8 (grammar+battery) + Wave 9 (recall) + Waves 24/25 (scored). *Terminus:* 100% reject on the battery AND 100% settle on the recall roster, closure-tested.\n- **P9 (provenance-binding contract)** â€” *value:* artifact = `{claim_id, domain, nonce, stdout_hash, exit_code, runtime_fingerprint}` from the Wave-9 subprocess [/ .olean / SMT cert in Increment-2]; canary re-execution = re-run the subprocess and compare the SHA-256 stdout hash; freshness = a **single-use claim-bound nonce = hash(claim_id + domain + monotone-counter)** where the monotone-counter is **DURABLE + monotone across restarts** (last-issued value per (claim_id,domain) persisted to the Phase-0 durability substrate â€” reuse, no new store; acceptable alt: a high-entropy per-mint random nonce + a persisted spent-nonce set the canary checks). **Write-ordering:** the counter-persist (or spent-nonce record) is ordered-BEFORE the artifact becomes valid, so a crash after mint but before flush leaves no usable replayable nonce on restart. Wave 2 round-trips the durable counter/spent-set across a simulated reload before Wave 4 relies on it. *Owner:* Wave 4 (+ Wave 2 substrate round-trip, Wave 6, Waves 24/25). *Terminus:* the E1 forged-artifact, cross-claim-replay, same-claim-replay, across-restart-replay, AND crash-mid-mint attempts are all rejected.\n- **P8 (SMT/cross-family integrity)** â€” *Increment-2 (Phase F).* *Value:* probabilistic-class integrity = N=5 trials at temp=0; pass-threshold = 5/5 reject of a known-FALSE sentinel + 5/5 accept